From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: Settings: disable Amlogic noise reduction by default

"Disable noise reduction" (label 14402) writes 0 to
/sys/module/aml_media/parameters/nr2_en, and only from
CWinSystemAmlogic::InitWindowSystem - so it takes effect at Kodi start and a
change from the default needs a restart to apply. On this hardware we always
want it off, so make that the shipped default rather than something to remember
to switch on after every reimage.

Default only: an install whose guisettings.xml already carries the setting keeps
whatever is in there.
---
--- a/system/settings/settings.xml
+++ b/system/settings/settings.xml
@@ -4119,7 +4119,7 @@
         <setting id="coreelec.amlogic.noisereduction" type="boolean" label="14402" help="14403">
           <requirement>HAVE_AMCODEC</requirement>
           <level>3</level>
-          <default>false</default>
+          <default>true</default>
           <control type="toggle" />
         </setting>
         <setting id="coreelec.amlogic.sdr2hdr" type="boolean" label="14404" help="14405">
